[32m+[m[32m## 1 — Platform Overview[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSentinelOps is a scoped ServiceNow application that enforces operational readiness governance before business services enter production. It answers one question: *Has this service been validated against all mandatory governance criteria before it can go live?*[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe application evaluates services against configurable governance policies, computes weighted readiness scores from structured checklist validation, enforces approval gates based on score outcomes and mandatory criterion results, and surfaces governance posture through dashboards — all within the ServiceNow platform.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### What Exists Today[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Layer | Artifact | Status |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Data Model | 5 tables, 3 roles, dictionary entries, choice lists, form layouts | ✅ Committed to SN source control |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Scoring Engine | `ReadinessScorer` Script Include — unweighted pass/total with mandatory override, 70% hardcoded threshold | ✅ Live in PDI, XML in `update/` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Checklist Generator | `ChecklistGenerator` Script Include — auto-creates `checklist_result` records from policy criteria | ✅ Live in PDI |[m
[32m+[m[32m| State Machine | 6-state lifecycle with `State Transition Guard` Business Rule using adjacency-list enforcement | ✅ Live in PDI, 16 revisions |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Score Recalculation | `Calculate Readiness Score` Business Rule — fires on `checklist_result` insert/update when `result` changes | ✅ Live in PDI |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Checklist Generation | `Generate Checklist Results` Business Rule — fires on `readiness_assessment` after insert | ✅ Live in PDI |[m
[32m+[m[32m| ACL Model | 24 table ACLs + associated role bindings across 4 primary tables, 4 condition scripts | ✅ Live in PDI |[m
[32m+[m[32m| REST API | `SentinelOps Ingestion` — POST `/api/x_1858206_sentin_0/sentinel_ops/submit` for release gate data | ✅ Live in PDI |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Release Gate Engine | `Evaluate Operational Governance` Business Rule on `release_gate` — threshold-based tech debt scoring | ✅ Live in PDI |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Cross-Scope Privileges | `GlideRecord.insert`, `GlideRecord.update`, `sys_choice` read, `Glide API: user roles and groups` | ✅ Configured |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Flow Designer | Assessment orchestration, CMDB validation subflow, score calculation subflow | ⬜ Design specs authored, not yet built |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Dashboards | 4 governance reports + dashboard assembly | ⬜ Phase 5 |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Design Philosophy[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSentinelOps is deliberately not a full GRC or ITOM platform. It is a focused governance gate — an enforcement point that sits between development completion and production promotion. The design follows three principles:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Auditable scoring.** Every gate outcome is traceable to individual criterion results. No black-box ML. The `ReadinessScorer` uses `Math.round((passed / total) * 100)` with a mandatory-fail override. An interviewer can read the algorithm in under 60 seconds.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Platform-native architecture.** Task extension, ACL condition scripts, Business Rule state enforcement, Flow Designer orchestration. No external dependencies, no custom UI frameworks, no integrations outside the ServiceNow instance.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Defense in depth.** Security is enforced at three layers simultaneously: ACL condition scripts (data layer), Business Rule state guards (logic layer), and UI Policies (presentation layer). A single bypass at any one layer does not compromise governance integrity.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2 — Governance Lifecycle and State Machine[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe assessment lifecycle is implemented as a finite state machine on the `state` field of `x_1858206_sentin_0_readiness_assessment`. State values are defined as ServiceNow choice list entries and enforced by the `State Transition Guard` Business Rule.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### State Values (from `author_elective_update/sys_choice_..._state.xml`)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| State | Value | Sequence | Terminal |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Draft | `1` | 100 | No |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Submitted | `10` | 200 | No |[m
[32m+[m[32m| In Review | `30` | 300 | No |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Approved | `40` | 400 | Yes |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Blocked | `50` | 500 | No |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Cancelled | `100` | 600 | Yes |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Transition Map (from `State Transition Guard` Business Rule)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe actual transition adjacency list as implemented in the production Business Rule:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```javascript[m
[32m+[m[32mvar allowed = {[m
[32m+[m[32m    '1':   ['10', '100'],              // Draft → Submitted, Cancelled[m
[32m+[m[32m    '10':  ['1', '30', '100'],         // Submitted → Draft, In Review, Cancelled[m
[32m+[m[32m    '30':  ['1', '10', '40', '50', '100'], // In Review → Draft, Submitted, Approved, Blocked, Cancelled[m
[32m+[m[32m    '40':  [],                         // Approved → nothing (terminal)[m
[32m+[m[32m    '50':  ['10', '100'],              // Blocked → Submitted (retry), Cancelled[m
[32m+[m[32m    '100': []                          // Cancelled → nothing (terminal)[m
[32m+[m[32m};[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m                    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐[m
[32m+[m[32m                    │                                                  ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mDraft (1) ──────► Submitted (10) ──────► In Review (30) ──────► Approved (40)[m
[32m+[m[32m  ▲                  │  ▲                  │  │  │                [terminal][m
[32m+[m[32m  │                  │  │                  │  │  │[m
[32m+[m[32m  │                  │  └──────────────────┘  │  └──────► Blocked (50)[m
[32m+[m[32m  │                  │                        │              │[m
[32m+[m[32m  │                  └──── (return to draft) ─┘              │[m
[32m+[m[32m  │                                                          ▼[m
[32m+[m[32m  └──────────────────────────────────────────────── Cancelled (100)[m
[32m+[m[32m                                                        [terminal][m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Enforcement Mechanism[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe guard runs as a **before** Business Rule on update (`order: 100`). If `current.state.changes()` is true and the target state is not in the allowed list for the current state, the rule calls `current.setAbortAction(true)` and adds an error message showing the attempted transition. The record is never saved.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mKey behaviors:[m
[32m+[m[32m- Unknown source states are **allowed** through as a safety valve (`if (!allowed[fromState]) return`)[m
[32m+[m[32m- Terminal states (Approved, Cancelled) have empty allowed-next arrays — no transitions are possible[m
[32m+[m[32m- Blocked assessments can retry submission (`50 → 10`) or be cancelled (`50 → 100`)[m
[32m+[m[32m- In Review allows regression to Draft (`30 → 1`) for rework — an intentional design decision[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
